From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:10:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8992: give pmsg more of the 2MB pstore reservation

The pstore region is 2MB, split console 1M / dump-records / ftrace 64K /
pmsg 512K. On a boot loop that pmsg ring wraps after a couple of cycles --
boot 9 ran ~19 system_server restarts and the ring no longer contained the
first crash, only the tail of the last cycle.

Raises pmsg to 832K out of the space that was going to spare dump records
(the remainder still leaves two 64K records, and we read kernel state from
console-ramoops anyway, not from the oops dumps).

Leaves ftrace at 64K rather than zeroing it: a zero-size zone is an untested
path in this 3.10-era pstore_ram driver and the 64K is not worth the risk.

This helps but does not solve the problem on its own -- see the device-side
adb diagnostic patch, which is the real fix.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/fih/nbq/msm8992-memory-pstore.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/fih/nbq/msm8992-memory-pstore.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/fih/nbq/msm8992-memory-pstore.dtsi
index ee6ba51000c..7e35b345985 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/fih/nbq/msm8992-memory-pstore.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/fih/nbq/msm8992-memory-pstore.dtsi
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 		android,ramoops-console-size = <0x100000>;
 		android,ramoops-record-size = <0x10000>;
 		android,ramoops-ftrace-size = <0x10000>;
-		android,ramoops-pmsg-size = <0x80000>;
+		android,ramoops-pmsg-size = <0xD0000>;
 		android,ramoops-dump-oops = <0x1>;
 	};
 };
